course: dictionary
lesson: 7288
title: Pioneers who go first
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pioneer is one of the first people to go somewhere new or to do something new. Other people often follow later. Context gives you clues: «Women have been part of computing from the start» tells you the start of something, so a pioneer is one of the first people in a field.
explain: The sentence says «Grace Hopper was a computing pioneer.» The words around it say computing began with women in the 1940s, so pioneer means one of the first to lead the way in computing. Check by swapping your meaning in: "Grace Hopper was one of the first to lead the way in computing" still makes sense.
explain: Pioneer can also be a verb, meaning to be the first to do, invent or use something. Pioneering, as an adjective, describes new work that leads the way. Words like these change their form, so look at the ending and the sentence to see which job the word is doing.
fact: A pioneer is one of the first people to explore or settle in a new land, or to do something new.
fact: «Pioneer» can also be a verb: to be the first to do, invent or use something.
fact: «Pioneering» means new and leading the way.
fact: «A pioneer of flight» means one of the first people to make flying possible.
fact: In plants, pioneer species are the first to grow on bare ground.
exercise: «Grace Hopper was a computing pioneer.» What does pioneer mean here? | A person who makes shoes | Someone who never tries anything new | *One of the first to lead the way in a field | A very slow type of computer
exercise: «Women have been part of computing from the start.» Find and copy one word that means the beginning. | *start | have | computing | part
exercise: Mia says a pioneer is a robot. What is the right meaning? | A type of old-fashioned hat | A person who follows the rules exactly | A machine that cleans floors | *One of the first people to explore or do something new
test: «The pioneering team built the first machine of its kind.» What does pioneering mean? | Lost in a forest | *New and leading the way | Angry at the machine | Very slow and old
test: Which sentence uses pioneer as a verb? | *They wanted to pioneer a new way to fly. | Two pioneers walked to the river. | The pioneers arrived in the valley in 1850. | Grace Hopper was a computing pioneer.
exam: In plants, what are pioneer species? | Plants that grow only in winter | Plants that are sold in shops | Plants that grow only in deep water | *The first plants to grow on bare ground
